  <name>Open Trofeo LCD</name>
  <summary>Linux driver and theme editor for Thermalright Trofeo LCD</summary>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-only</project_license>
  <developer_name>Abigor-DIY</developer_name>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.abigordiy.open-trofeo-lcd.desktop</launchable>
  <pkgname>open-trofeo-lcd</pkgname>
  <icon type="stock">io.github.abigordiy.open-trofeo-lcd</icon>
  <categories>
    <category>Settings</category>
    <category>HardwareSettings</category>
  </categories>
  <provides>
    <modalias>usb:v0416p5408d*</modalias>
  </provides>
  <developer id="io.github.abigordiy">
    <name>Abigor-DIY</name>
  </developer>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/Abigor-DIY/Open-Trofeo-LCD</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/Abigor-DIY/Open-Trofeo-LCD/issues</url>
  <description>
    <p>
      Open Trofeo LCD is a reverse-engineered Linux driver and desktop editor
      for the Thermalright Trofeo LCD cooler display.
    </p>
    <p>
      The native package installs a user backend service, udev rules for the
      Trofeo LCD USB device, and a desktop editor. The application talks to the
      LCD over local USB, reads desktop media metadata through MPRIS, and uses
      the network only for optional weather data and future online theme
      features.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a development preview. The backend, USB transfer path, Theme
      Gallery, Theme Designer, Animation Studio and packaging flow are still
      being refined.
    </p>
  </description>
